    "https://careers.jsu.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-music-industry-fall-2026-spring-2027-jacksonville-al-main-campus-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty- Music Industry (Fall 2026 - Spring 2027) - Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Back to JSU My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Adjunct Faculty- Music Industry (Fall 2026 - Spring 2027) Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States, 36265 Adjunct Add to favorites View favorites Adjunct Faculty Position Music Department Music Industry Job Summary The Department of Music at Jacksonville State University (Jax State) invites applications for an adjunct music industry instructor. The successful applicant will teach courses such as music industry history, contemporary issues and trends in the music industry, marketing/entrepreneurship, and arts management. Our department offers undergraduate programs of study in Music Education, Music Industry, Music Performance, and General Music. In addition, the department offers graduate programs in General Music and Music Education. A minimum of 18 graduate hours in the discipline is required. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities The successful candidate should have knowledge of the structure of the music industry, knowledge of record labels and music licensing agencies, digital content creation and distribution, and the fundamentals of arts management which includes US copyright law. Necessary skills for a music industry instructor include the ability to analyze industry data and trends, operate production software, interpret contract language and design agreements, coordinate music events and effectively demonstrate how to manage budgets and finances. Teach undergraduate students in the following courses: The History of the Music Industry, Music Licensing & Intellectual Property, Contemporary Issues in the Music Industry, and Arts Management and Concert Production. Minimum Qualifications Minimum of 18 credit hours in the discipline or related field Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in discipline and industry experience in management, production, publishing or marketing Required Application Documents Cover letter addressing qualifications Teaching philosophy. Curriculum vitae or resume. Contact information for three professional references. About Jax State Located in the Appalachian foothills of northeast Alabama, midway between Birmingham and Atlanta, Jax State is home to over 10,000 students representing 63 countries. As a learning-centered university, it strives to challenge students academically in a responsive environment, meeting their educational, career, and personal goals. As an academic institution, it aims to produce broadly educated graduates who are prepared for global engagement. As a public, comprehensive university, it promotes excellence in scholarly and service activities consistent with its academic and professional strengths. For a complete list of Goals, Core Values, and Strategies to fulfill this Mission, go to the JSU Strategic Plan home page. Academically, Jax State offers 113 academic programs and concentrations, including bachelor's, master's, post-baccalaureate, doctoral, and advanced certificate programs in a variety of disciplines that prepare graduates for meaningful careers and ongoing education.  More than 40 online programs are offered.  The University features six colleges on its 459-acre campus – Arts, Humanities and Sciences; Business and Industry; Education and Professional Studies; Health Professions and Wellness; Social and Behavioral Sciences; and Library. Most academic programs have discipline-specific accreditations, a reflection of their quality and JSU’s commitment to excellence. Clery Notice: In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, https://www.clerycenter.org/the-clery-act the Jacksonville State University Police provide information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three calendar years. The JSU Annual Campus Security and Fire Report is available online at: http://jsu.edu/police/docs/CleryAnnualReport.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity: Jax State is an Equal Employment and Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4d44a714 Last Name (required) 62322917 Email (required) 9e6a8ebc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Auxiliary Teacher, 1 Year Olds Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Education and Professional Studies The auxiliary teacher will assist with implementing a model Pre-K program for a group of children and provide support to the lead teacher with the following: planning and implementing appropriate activities for children, working with faculty and administration, working with families of young children, and modeling evidence-based practices in the classroom for early educator observers, graduate, and undergraduate students.\n\nThis position is a 9-month, bi-weekly payroll position working 187 days per year. Transfer Admissions Counselor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Enrollment Mgmt The Transfer Admissions Counselor advises and counsels prospective students about the college selection process and the benefits of a Jax State education in their geographical and admit-type territory. They also continuously represent the University in a positive professional manner. This position is responsible for assisting the Associate Director in the development and implementation of strategic enrollment planning for recruitment initiatives for Jax State. The position serves as the primary point of contact students and provides technical assistance and serves as a resource person for students, staff, and faculty. Maintenance Inventory Clerk II Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Finance & Admin The Maintenance Inventory Clerk II in Capital Planning and Facilities performs routine work in the operation of a maintenance stock room.  This includes manual and clerical tasks in the receiving, storing, inventorying, and care of supplies, parts and other tools and equipment required for the maintenance department of the University.  Work is reviewed while in progress and upon completion for compliance. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert fd92edbb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Adjunct Adjunct Locations Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States First Name (required) 62c95d40 Last Name (required) c62bffc1 Email (required) c5297594 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 700 Pelham Rd N Jacksonville, AL 36265 Phone: 1-800-231-5291 or 1-256-782-5781 Email: info@jsu.edu Facebook Youtube Instagram © 2026 Jacksonville State University Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
