    "https://careers.jsu.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-aviation-fall-2026-spring-2027-jacksonville-al-main-campus-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Aviation (Fall 2026 - Spring 2027) - Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Back to JSU My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Adjunct Faculty - Aviation (Fall 2026 - Spring 2027) Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States, 36265 Adjunct Add to favorites View favorites Adjunct Faculty Position Aviation Department Job Summary The Aviation Program at Jacksonville State University (JSU) invites applications for qualified adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate courses in Aviation. Courses may be offered in face-to-face, hybrid, or online formats depending on program needs. Adjunct faculty are expected to provide high-quality instruction that supports student learning and aligns with program and university standards. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Adjunct faculty members are responsible for teaching assigned aviation courses and may be asked to instruct specialized topics within the Aviation curriculum. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Preparing and delivering course content aligned with approved syllabi and learning outcomes Providing instruction in areas such as aviation meteorology, aerodynamics, aircraft systems, navigation, aviation regulations, safety, human factors, air traffic control, or other aviation-related topics Maintaining accurate records for attendance, assessments, and grades Submitting grades and required documentation by university deadlines Using the university’s learning management system for course delivery and communication, as applicable Required Qualifications Applicants must meet one or more of the following qualification pathways to be considered: Bachelor’s degree in Aviation, Aeronautical Science, Aerospace, or a closely related field with demonstrated professional expertise in aviation, or Training and experience in aviation sufficient to qualify the individual to teach specific aviation courses, consistent with university and accreditation standards In addition, candidates must demonstrate direct education and/or professional experience related to the aviation topics they are expected to teach. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Aviation, Aeronautical Science, or a related discipline Current or prior FAA certifications such as Certified Flight Instructor (CFI), Certified Flight Instructor–Instrument (CFII), Ground Instructor (GI/AGI), or Airline Transport Pilot (ATP) Professional flight or aviation industry experience (e.g., Part 61, Part 135, Part 121, military aviation, airport operations, or aviation management) College or university teaching experience Experience teaching in online or hybrid learning environments Required Application Materials Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Department Information The Aviation Program at Jacksonville State University prepares students for professional careers in the aviation industry through a combination of academic coursework, applied learning, and industry-informed instruction. The program emphasizes safety, technical proficiency, regulatory knowledge, and professional preparation. About Jax State Located in the Appalachian foothills of northeast Alabama, midway between Birmingham and Atlanta, Jax State is home to over 10,000 students representing 63 countries. As a learning-centered university, it strives to challenge students academically in a responsive environment, meeting their educational, career, and personal goals. As an academic institution, it aims to produce broadly educated graduates who are prepared for global engagement. As a public, comprehensive university, it promotes excellence in scholarly and service activities consistent with its academic and professional strengths. For a complete list of Goals, Core Values, and Strategies to fulfill this Mission, go to the JSU Strategic Plan home page. Academically, Jax State offers 113 academic programs and concentrations, including bachelor's, master's, post-baccalaureate, doctoral, and advanced certificate programs in a variety of disciplines that prepare graduates for meaningful careers and ongoing education.  More than 40 online programs are offered.  The University features six colleges on its 459-acre campus – Arts, Humanities and Sciences; Business and Industry; Education and Professional Studies; Health Professions and Wellness; Social and Behavioral Sciences; and Library. Most academic programs have discipline-specific accreditations, a reflection of their quality and JSU’s commitment to excellence. Clery Notice: In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, https://www.clerycenter.org/the-clery-act the Jacksonville State University Police provide information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three calendar years. The JSU Annual Campus Security and Fire Report is available online at: http://jsu.edu/police/docs/CleryAnnualReport.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity: Jax State is an Equal Employment and Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 26d95519 Last Name (required) 9e69822e Email (required) 159acb28 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Auxiliary Teacher, 1 Year Olds Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Education and Professional Studies The auxiliary teacher will assist with implementing a model Pre-K program for a group of children and provide support to the lead teacher with the following: planning and implementing appropriate activities for children, working with faculty and administration, working with families of young children, and modeling evidence-based practices in the classroom for early educator observers, graduate, and undergraduate students.\n\nThis position is a 9-month, bi-weekly payroll position working 187 days per year. Transfer Admissions Counselor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Enrollment Mgmt The Transfer Admissions Counselor advises and counsels prospective students about the college selection process and the benefits of a Jax State education in their geographical and admit-type territory. They also continuously represent the University in a positive professional manner. This position is responsible for assisting the Associate Director in the development and implementation of strategic enrollment planning for recruitment initiatives for Jax State. The position serves as the primary point of contact students and provides technical assistance and serves as a resource person for students, staff, and faculty. Maintenance Inventory Clerk II Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Finance & Admin The Maintenance Inventory Clerk II in Capital Planning and Facilities performs routine work in the operation of a maintenance stock room.  This includes manual and clerical tasks in the receiving, storing, inventorying, and care of supplies, parts and other tools and equipment required for the maintenance department of the University.  Work is reviewed while in progress and upon completion for compliance. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 425836a0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Adjunct Adjunct Locations Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States First Name (required) 4c76ae29 Last Name (required)