    "https://careers.jsu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-graphic-design-jacksonville-al-main-campus-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Graphic Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Graphic Design - Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Back to JSU My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Professor, Graphic Design Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States, 36265 Faculty 9-Month Add to favorites View favorites Jacksonville State University Professor of Art, Graphic Design Named Alabama's #1 employer for 2025 by Forbes Magazine! Read more here ! Jacksonville State University is seeking applicants for a tenure-track position in Visual Communication/Graphic Design at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. The selected candidate will be expected to teach a 3/3 load at all levels of visual communication design from undergraduate to graduate, fully engage in departmental duties, committee work, campus activities, and scholarship/creative activity. The Department of Art + Design at Jacksonville State University, is accredited by NASAD, and offers an MFA in Visual Communication Design and a BFA degrees in Studio Art with concentrations in Ceramics, Illustration, Graphic Design, Painting, Photography, and Printmaking. The department also offers a BA in Art History and Art Minors in Studio Art, Photography, and Art History. The Visual Communication/Graphic Design program at JSU is competitive, and fosters a culture of passion, craftsmanship, and an atmosphere of play. Both graduate and undergraduate design students are winning regional, national, and international awards. Physical Requirements: Teaching requires time with students in the studio and labs. Candidates should be able to prepare and present assignments and evaluate students’ work in progress. A successful candidate should be available for advising and mentoring students during office hours and as needed. Candidates should be able to move between art buildings and administrative buildings on campus for meetings. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Successful candidates must demonstrate a broad understanding of contemporary design practice and theory, as well as proficiency with current industry-standard software. They should show mastery of formal design principles, typography, and layout in both their own work and their students’ work. Minimum Qualifications: This position requires an MFA or MDes from a regionally accredited institution in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, or similar design degree. Experience using current Adobe Creative Suite is required. Instructions to Applicants: To demonstrate a record of professional and creative accomplishment, creative work samples are required to be submitted in a digital portfolio. Submission of 20 samples of creative work in pdf or URL format, and 20 samples of students' work in pdf or URL format are required. Send pdf or URL to blafferty@jsu.edu . If samples of student work are unavailable, please explain in the cover letter. Application must be made on-line at with a curriculum vita, research statement, teaching philosophy, cover letter, and unofficial copies of transcripts. Review of applications will begin November 17, 2025, with on-campus interviews beginning in January 2026. The position has an anticipated start date of August 1, 2026. About Jax State Located in the Appalachian foothills of northeast Alabama, midway between Birmingham and Atlanta, Jax State is home to more than 10,300 students representing 63 countries. As a learning-centered university, it strives to challenge students academically in a responsive environment, meeting their educational, career and personal goals. As an academic institution, it seeks to produce broadly educated graduates prepared for global engagement. As a public, comprehensive university, it promotes excellence in scholarly and service activities consistent with its academic and professional strengths. For a complete list of Goals, Core Values and Strategies to fulfill this Mission, go to the JSU Strategic Plan home page. Academically Jax State offers 113 academic programs and concentrations, including bachelor's, master's, post-baccalaureate, doctoral and advanced certificate programs in a variety of disciplines that prepare graduates for meaningful careers and ongoing education.  More than 40 online programs are offered.  The University features six colleges on its 459-acre campus – Arts, Humanities and Sciences; Business and Industry; Education and Professional Studies; Health Professions and Wellness; Social and Behavioral Sciences; and Library. Most academic programs have discipline-specific accreditations, a reflection of their quality and JSU’s commitment to excellence. Clery Notice: In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, https://www.clerycenter.org/the-clery-act the Jacksonville State University Police provide information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three calendar years. The JSU Annual Campus Security and Fire Report is available online at: https://www.jsu.edu/police/docs/CleryAnnualReport.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity: Jax State is an Equal Employment and Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 2c23a444 Last Name (required) 67a25247 Email (required) 3386e1e5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Auxiliary Teacher, 1 Year Olds Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Education and Professional Studies The auxiliary teacher will assist with implementing a model Pre-K program for a group of children and provide support to the lead teacher with the following: planning and implementing appropriate activities for children, working with faculty and administration, working with families of young children, and modeling evidence-based practices in the classroom for early educator observers, graduate, and undergraduate students.\n\nThis position is a 9-month, bi-weekly payroll position working 187 days per year. Transfer Admissions Counselor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Enrollment Mgmt The Transfer Admissions Counselor advises and counsels prospective students about the college selection process and the benefits of a Jax State education in their geographical and admit-type territory. They also continuously represent the University in a positive professional manner. This position is responsible for assisting the Associate Director in the development and implementation of strategic enrollment planning for recruitment initiatives for Jax State. The position serves as the primary point of contact students and provides technical assistance and serves as a resource person for students, staff, and faculty. Maintenance Inventory Clerk II Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Finance & Admin The Maintenance Inventory Clerk II in Capital Planning and Facilities performs routine work in the operation of a maintenance stock room.  This includes manual and clerical tasks in the receiving, storing, inventorying, and care of supplies, parts and other tools and equipment required for the maintenance department of the University.  Work is reviewed while in progress and upon completion for compliance. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert ae8486ec Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Faculty 9-Month Faculty 9-Month Locations Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United 