    "https://careers.jsu.edu/jobs/instructor-or-assistant-professor-master-s-in-athletic-training-program-jacksonville-al-main-campus-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Athletic Training",
      "description": "Instructor or Assistant Professor, Master's in Athletic Training Program - Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Back to JSU My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Instructor or Assistant Professor, Master's in Athletic Training Program Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States, 36265 Faculty 9-Month Add to favorites View favorites Jacksonville State University Instructor or Assistant Professor of Athletic Training Jacksonville State University’s College of Health Professions & Wellness invites applications for a full-time, 9-month faculty position in Athletic Training. The successful candidate will contribute to the teaching, service, and program development needs of the Master Athletic Training (MAT) program. This is a 9-month faculty position. Appointment will be made at the Instructor level for candidates with a master’s degree, or at the Assistant Professor level (tenure track) for candidates who hold an earned Doctorate degree. The successful candidate will contribute to the teaching, service, and program development needs of the Master Athletic Training (MAT) program, and the Department of Kinesiology programs as needed. ‑time, 9‑month faculty position in Athletic Training. The successful candidate will contribute to the teaching, service, and program development needs of the Master Athletic Training (MAT) program. Appointment will be made at the Instructor level for candidates with a master’s degree, or at the Assistant Professor level (tenure‑track) for candidates who hold an earned doctorate. We are seeking a dynamic educator with clinical experience who is committed to excellence in teaching, student engagement, and advancing the mission of a growing, collaborative program dedicated to preparing highly skilled athletic training professionals. Primary Responsibilities Teach graduate-level coursework within the MAT curriculum in areas such as clinical practice, therapeutic interventions, examination and diagnosis, emergency care, and evidence-based practice. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the Kinesiology department. Supervise and mentor students during clinical education experiences. Contribute to program assessment, accreditation processes (CAATE), and curriculum development. Engage in university, college, and departmental service activities. For tenure track Assistant Professor candidates: maintain an active scholarly agenda and participate in research, presentations, or professional activities. ‑track Assistant Professor candidates: maintain an active scholarly agenda and participate in research, presentations, or professional activities. Candidates: maintain an active scholarly agenda and participate in research, presentations, or professional activities. Support recruitment and retention initiatives for the MAT program. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in athletic training or related field (Instructor rank). If the candidate’s master’s degree is in a related field, candidate must hold a bachelor’s degree in athletic training. Doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DAT, or related) from an accredited institution for consideration at the Assistant Professor, tenure track rank. Current BOC certification and eligibility for Alabama state licensure. Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching, precepting, or professional practice in athletic training. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Prior college or university teaching experience in a variety of modes of delivery. Experience with CAATE accreditation standards and assessment practices. Evidence of scholarly engagement (for tenure track candidates).track candidates). Clinical expertise in one or more areas such as orthopedics, rehabilitation, or emergency management. Applicants should submit: A cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. This position has an anticipated start date of August 1, 2026. About Jacksonville, Alabama Jacksonville offers an exceptional quality of life in the heart of Alabama's scenic Appalachian foothills. Located strategically between Birmingham and Atlanta, residents enjoy easy access to major metropolitan areas while embracing the charm of a vibrant college town. The area boasts beautiful natural landscapes with numerous parks, hiking trails, and outdoor recreation opportunities at nearby Cheaha State Park and Talladega National Forest. Jacksonville features a thriving downtown district with local restaurants, shops, and cultural venues, complemented by excellent schools and family-friendly neighborhoods. The cost of living is remarkably affordable compared to major metropolitan areas, allowing for a comfortable lifestyle with access to quality healthcare, recreational facilities, and a strong sense of community. The region's rich history, combined with Jacksonville State University's cultural and athletic events, creates a dynamic environment that attracts professionals seeking both career growth and an outstanding work-life balance. About Jacksonville State University Located in the Appalachian foothills of northeast Alabama, Jax State is home to over 10,000 students representing 63 countries. As a learning-centered university, it strives to challenge students academically in a responsive environment, meeting their educational, career and personal goals. Academically, Jax State offers 113 academic programs and concentrations, including bachelor's, master's, post-baccalaureate, doctoral and advanced certificate programs. More than 40 online programs are offered across six colleges on its 459-acre campus. For more details about Jacksonville, AL, please click on this link . Clery Notice: In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, https://www.clerycenter.org/the-clery-act the Jacksonville State University Police provide information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three calendar years. The JSU Annual Campus Security and Fire Report is available at: https://www.jsu.edu/police/docs/cleryannualreport.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity: Jax State is an Equal Employment and Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4ef08f2c Last Name (required) 1daa3054 Email (required) 7957a5d7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Auxiliary Teacher, 1 Year Olds Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Education and Professional Studies The auxiliary teacher will assist with implementing a model Pre-K program for a group of children and provide support to the lead teacher with the following: planning and implementing appropriate activities for children, working with faculty and administration, working with families of young children, and modeling evidence-based practices in the classroom for early educator observers, graduate, and undergraduate students.\n\nThis position is a 9-month, bi-weekly payroll position working 187 days per year. Transfer Admissions Counselor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Enrollment Mgmt The Transfer Admissions Counselor advises and counsels prospective students about the college selection process and the benefits of a Jax State education in their geographical and admit-type territory. They also continuously represent the University in a positive professional manner. This position is responsible for assisting the Associate Director in the development and implementation of strategic enrollment planning for recruitment initiatives for Jax State. The position serves as the primary point of contact students and provides technical assistance and serves as a resource person for students, staff, and faculty. Maintenance Inventory Clerk II Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Finance & Admin The Maintenance Inventory Clerk II in Capital Planning and Facilities performs routine work in the operation of a maintenance stock room.  This includes manual and clerical tasks in the receiving, storing, inventorying, and care of supplies, parts and other tools and equipment required for the maintenance department of the University.  Work is reviewed while in progress and upon completion for compliance. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 0b8646ea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Faculty 9-Month Faculty 9-Month Locations Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States First Name (required) f3b5a7ef Last Name (required) 4a90574c Email (required) a4f0e5e2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 700 Pelham Rd N Jacksonville, AL 36265 Phone: 1-800-231-5291 or 1-256-782-5781 Email: info@jsu.edu Facebook Youtube Instagram © 2026 Jacksonville State University Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
