    "https://careers.jsu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-sports-industry-jacksonville-al-main-campus-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Sports Industry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Sports Industry - Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Back to JSU My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Professor, Sports Industry Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States, 36265 Faculty 9-Month Add to favorites View favorites Jacksonville State University Assistant Professor, Sports Industry The Department of Kinesiology in Jacksonville State University’s College of Health Professions and Wellness invites applications for two Assistant Professor positions within the Sports Industry program. The Sports Industry Assistant Professors in the Department of Kinesiology, provide educational services to traditional and non-traditional students during the day or evening; teaching undergraduate and graduate level courses in Kinesiology, and may be required to teach courses within their concentration area on campus, off-campus, online courses and possible videoconferencing depending on need of location The Jacksonville State University College of Health Professions and Wellness was established to deliver a top-quality education for 21st century professionals to promote health and wellness in our communities, state, nation, and around the world.  The departments of nursing, respiratory therapy, and kinesiology have developed undergraduate and graduate programs utilizing the latest evidence-based practices.  It is our goal to prepare future leaders in health and wellness professions. Position Requirements Earned doctorate in Sport Management or closely related field from an accredited institution (ABD candidates near completion will be considered) Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching at the university level. Evidence of a promising research agenda and scholarly publications Strong communication and interpersonal skills Commitment to fostering an inclusive and diverse academic environment. Preference may be given to those who possess the following. Experience with COSMA (Commission on Sport Management Accreditation) processes and standards Industry experience in sport management or related fields Expertise in one or more of the following areas: sport marketing, sport communication, sport finance, sport law, sport management, or sport analytics Experience with online and hybrid course delivery Record of successful grant writing or external funding acquisition Applicants must submit a cover letter, resume or CV, teaching philosophy and unofficial transcripts to be considered for the position.  Official transcripts will be required upon hire. This position has an anticipated start date of August 1, 2026. About Jax State Located in the Appalachian foothills of northeast Alabama, midway between Birmingham and Atlanta, Jax State is home to over 10,000 students representing 63 countries. As a learning-centered university, it strives to challenge students academically in a responsive environment, meeting their educational, career, and personal goals. As an academic institution, it aims to produce broadly educated graduates who are prepared for global engagement. As a public, comprehensive university, it promotes excellence in scholarly and service activities consistent with its academic and professional strengths. For a complete list of Goals, Core Values, and Strategies to fulfill this Mission, go to the JSU Strategic Plan home page . Academically, Jax State offers 113 academic programs and concentrations, including bachelor's, master's, post-baccalaureate, doctoral, and advanced certificate programs in a variety of disciplines that prepare graduates for meaningful careers and ongoing education.  More than 40 online programs are offered.  The University features six colleges on its 459-acre campus – Arts, Humanities and Sciences; Business and Industry; Education and Professional Studies; Health Professions and Wellness; Social and Behavioral Sciences; and Library. Most academic programs have discipline-specific accreditations, a reflection of their quality and JSU’s commitment to excellence. Clery Notice: In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, https://www.clerycenter.org/the-clery-act the Jacksonville State University Police provide information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three calendar years. The JSU Annual Campus Security and Fire Report is available at: https://www.jsu.edu/police/docs/cleryannualreport.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity: Jax State is an Equal Employment and Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) a111e23b Last Name (required) 3fe05c07 Email (required) 28379dab Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Auxiliary Teacher, 1 Year Olds Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Education and Professional Studies The auxiliary teacher will assist with implementing a model Pre-K program for a group of children and provide support to the lead teacher with the following: planning and implementing appropriate activities for children, working with faculty and administration, working with families of young children, and modeling evidence-based practices in the classroom for early educator observers, graduate, and undergraduate students.\n\nThis position is a 9-month, bi-weekly payroll position working 187 days per year. Transfer Admissions Counselor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Enrollment Mgmt The Transfer Admissions Counselor advises and counsels prospective students about the college selection process and the benefits of a Jax State education in their geographical and admit-type territory. They also continuously represent the University in a positive professional manner. This position is responsible for assisting the Associate Director in the development and implementation of strategic enrollment planning for recruitment initiatives for Jax State. The position serves as the primary point of contact students and provides technical assistance and serves as a resource person for students, staff, and faculty. Maintenance Inventory Clerk II Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Finance & Admin The Maintenance Inventory Clerk II in Capital Planning and Facilities performs routine work in the operation of a maintenance stock room.  This includes manual and clerical tasks in the receiving, storing, inventorying, and care of supplies, parts and other tools and equipment required for the maintenance department of the University.  Work is reviewed while in progress and upon completion for compliance. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 3a5e43ea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Faculty 9-Month Faculty 9-Month Locations Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States First Name (required) eaaabb3f Last Name (required) 9e487c34 Email (required) 19ed2169 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 700 Pelham Rd N Jacksonville, AL 36265 Phone: 1-800-231-5291 or 1-256-782-5781 Email: info@jsu.edu Facebook Youtube Instagram © 2026 Jacksonville State University Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect